# Booking Hub Project Rules
# These rules apply to every code suggestion in this project

## 1. FILE CHANGES
- Always provide FULL file contents — never just snippets
- Show exactly what to REMOVE and what to ADD
- Regenerate the entire file when changes are needed

## 2. PACKAGE SAFETY
- Before suggesting ANY npm package, confirm:
  - No critical vulnerabilities in the last 6 months
  - More than 100,000 weekly downloads on npm
  - Actively maintained (last commit within 30 days)
- Approved packages: express, cors, helmet, morgan, dotenv, nodemon, supabase, axios, react-router-dom
- Avoid: any package with <10k weekly downloads or known security issues

## 3. USER INPUT VALIDATION
- Every function that accepts user input MUST have:
  - Validation check before processing
  - A friendly error message showing what went wrong
  - Example: "Please enter a valid email address" instead of "Invalid input"

## 4. NETWORK REQUEST ERROR HANDLING
- Every network request (fetch, axios, API calls) MUST have:
  - A .catch() block or try/catch wrapper
  - Error message: "Something went wrong. Please try again."
  - Console.error for debugging

## 5. BOOKING PAYLOAD CONTRACT
- The booking payload structure is LOCKED:
  {
    date: "YYYY-MM-DD",
    email: "user@example.com",
    service: "hotel" | "sports" | "event"
  }
- Do NOT add, remove, or rename these fields without explicit permission

## 6. API ENDPOINT STRUCTURE
- All API endpoints MUST start with /api/
- Examples: /api/bookings, /api/businesses, /api/admin
- Do NOT create endpoints without the /api/ prefix

## 7. COMMUNICATION STYLE
- Explain concepts like I'm a business analyst learning to code
- No jargon without explanation
- One plain-English sentence explaining the root cause first
- Then provide the solution

## 8. EXISTING FUNCTIONALITY PROTECTION
- Never break existing features when adding new ones
- Test mentally that old flows still work before suggesting changes
- If a change might affect something else, warn me first

## 9. FILE ORGANIZATION
- Frontend: client/src/
- Backend: server/src/
- New components go in appropriate folders
- Reusable utilities go in a utils/ or services/ folder

## 10. DEMO CREDENTIALS (Never Change These)
- Admin: admin@booking.com / admin123
- Business Owner: test@hotel.com / any password
- Staff: manager@testhotel.com / manager123